    <main>
        <h1>LeetCode 3693: Climbing Stairs II (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                You are climbing a staircase with n + 1 steps, numbered from 0 to n. You are given a
                1-indexed integer array costs of length n, where costs[i] is the cost of step i. From step i,
                you can jump only to step i + 1, i + 2, or i + 3. The cost of jumping from step i to step j
                is costs[j] + (j - i)^2. You start from step 0 with cost = 0. Return the minimum total cost
                to reach step n.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: n = 4, costs = [1,2,3,4]<br>
                Output: 13<br>
                Explanation: One optimal path is 0 → 1 → 2 → 4. Jumping 0 → 1 costs 1 + 1 = 2, jumping
                1 → 2 costs 2 + 1 = 3, and jumping 2 → 4 costs 4 + 4 = 8, for a total of 13.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    static int climbStairs(int n, vector&lt;int&gt;&amp; costs) {
        int dp[4] = {0}, ans = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i &lt; n; i++) {
            const int idx = i &amp; 3, cost = costs[i];
            int curr = dp[(idx + 3) &amp; 3] + 1;
            curr = min(curr, dp[(idx + 2) &amp; 3] + 4);
            curr = min(curr, dp[(idx + 1) &amp; 3] + 9);
            dp[idx] = ans = cost + curr;
        }
        return ans;
    }
};</code></pre>
